        ":question/id": "db3973ed-197d-5377-b8db-60e027e16ad0",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-47983",
        ":question/problem": "Find the derivative of $y=\\sqrt{x}+tan\u2061x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(tan\u2061x)={sec}^{2}\u2061x.$ Applying this formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}+tan\u2061x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+{sec}^{2}\u2061x \\\\  & =\\frac{1+2\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}\u2061x}{2\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
